    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The fix has been successfully implemented and compiled. The change I made:\n\n1. **Identified the issue**: The `gate` command in frai-cli was using Commander's variadic arguments `[args...]`, which don't capture flag arguments like `--ci`. The flag was being silently dropped.\n\n2. **Implemented the fix**: Instead of relying on the `args` parameter, I now use `process.argv` directly to capture all arguments passed after the 'gate' command, including flags:\n   ```typescript\n   const gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\n   const allArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];\n   const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...allArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n   ```\n\n3. **Rebuilt the package**: Used `pnpm --filter frai build` to compile the TypeScript changes.\n\nThe compiled JavaScript (lines 635-637 in dist/index.js) now correctly passes all arguments including `--ci` to the frai-gate CLI, which will properly create both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`.",
